Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:21:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(release): v4.2 notes describe only what shipped, record
 the release, point adopters at the checkout

Addresses the review of this PR:

- README.md and CLAUDE.md no longer present two defects as fixed by v4.2. Running the clone's
  manifest and the seed-relabel overwrite existed only in 9b69070 on the PR #91 branch, which is not
  in v4.1; they were removed in fa44be6 before the merge. The bullets now say why the manifest is
  read as data and what the refusal prevents.
- CHANGELOG.md gains the release's own entry (tag type, commit, publish time, gate line), as v3.8,
  v4.0 and v4.1 have.
- The adopter line says that sync itself delivers only the 2.11.3 dashboard: nothing under bin/ is
  distributed, so D8 reaches an adopter when they update their methodology checkout.
- Wording: "is or lies inside .git" and "names no file (.)"; the merge date is 2026-10-02; the three
  non-blocking points are the approval round's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
