 - **v4.1:** **Fan-out to many agents becomes a named session shape — many hands, one closer, one writer per working tree.** The parallel-sessions plan (`docs/planning/parallel-sessions-plan.md`, PR #83; its twelve decisions ratified with amendments in §8A by S27 under the operator's delegation) implemented in sessions S28–S36. **(1) The contract** — `ITERATIVE_METHODOLOGY.md` §Parallel Actors: Shape A, one session with many hands (the vertical-slice gates a–d plus (e) one closer, (f) disjoint write scopes, (g) serial integration), and Shape B, many sessions on their own branches or worktrees joined by merge (`S<N>-<seq>` identities off the trunk, a merge as one action with one receipt and a merged-PR ledger check, cross-line scoring); Principle 9 gains *many hands, one closer*; **FM #29 "Shared-state interference"** appended (FMs 1–28 byte-unchanged; **the count moves 28 → 29**) with its Degradation row; a SAFEGUARDS Blast-Radius row, *one writer per working tree*; **Learning #17**. The runner and SAFEGUARDS additions were paid by reduction and measured by doubled reads: the pair reads 24,844.5 tokens, under the 25,000 read cap, where a draft the density estimate passed had read over it. **(2) The ledgers merge** — new SEED `starter-kit/gitattributes` → `.gitattributes` (`bin/_manifest.py` 29 → 30): `merge=union` for `CHANGELOG.md` and the two `.jsonl` histories, deliberately **not** `HANDOFFS.md` — measured: union fuses two prepended receipts into one block at exit 0 under git's default and `zdiff3` styles — whose conflicts resolve keep-both with `git merge-file --union --diff3`. GitHub's merge button ignores the driver (measured on probe PR #90): merge locally. New canonical-only `bin/check-ledger`, declared as a 12th gate in `.quality-gates.json`; `bin/check-handoff` refuses a key repeated in one block (a fused receipt had passed as one clean receipt) and accepts one live pending receipt per line of sessions; the canonical pre-commit hook refuses an edit to a committed `CHANGELOG.md` entry. **(3) Tools** — `context_budget.py` 1.3.1 finds a project's transcripts from a linked worktree; `DASHBOARD_VERSION` 2.11.1 → 2.11.2 (accounts for the new seed). **(4) Both shapes dogfooded** — the docs sweep ran as a Shape A fan-out (four read-only workers returning content; 0 of their claims wrong on re-derivation), and two concurrent sessions ran in linked worktrees and were merged locally (exit 0, then exit 1 on `HANDOFFS.md` alone, resolved by the recipe); the one defect they found — a merging session's early claim failing every concurrent line's receipt check — is the per-line pending rule above. Housekeeping: `CHANGELOG.md` trimmed into `docs/archive/`, PR #77 backfilled. **Not in this release:** D8 (`--source=github` iterates the source's manifest) awaits review in PR #91. **Adopters** receive the flight-manual section, runner and SAFEGUARDS changes and the `.gitattributes` seed — only where no `.gitattributes` exists, otherwise `BOOTSTRAP.md` Step 10 gives the three lines; the `HANDOFFS.md` seed's new paragraph reaches new projects only, and the rule it states lives in the synced flight manual. `bin/tests.sh` 215 → 243. **No phase, no quality gate of the twelve, no workstream change; Principle 9 amended by one paragraph and Phase 1 step 4 by one clause; the failure-mode count moves 28 → 29.** Shipped as annotated tag + GitHub Release `v4.1`.
 
-- **v4.2:** **`--source=github` installs from the source's own manifest** — D8 of the parallel-sessions plan, the item v4.1 left out (PR #91, rmsharp's review: three non-blocking points, all addressed before merge on 2026-10-03). `bin/sync` and `bin/status` read the manifest of the repository they clone instead of this checkout's, so a source newer than the checkout installs its own file list. **The manifest is read as data, never run:** new `bin/_manifest_reader.py` parses the clone's `bin/_manifest.py` with `ast` and takes `DISTRIBUTION`, `SEED_FORMAT_MARKERS` and the two label strings as literals, which is why `_manifest.py` is documented as literal data, one plain assignment per name. **Unsafe rows are refused before anything is written:** a disposition other than this checkout's `tracked` or `seed` stops the run and names the rows (a source labelling seeds differently had overwritten an adopter's `CHANGELOG.md` at exit 0 with no `--force`; `bin/status` read an unknown label as a seed and under-reported drift, and now refuses the same way); a `src` or `dest` that is absolute, has a drive letter, climbs out with `..`, is `.git` or `.`, or contains a NUL byte is refused, as is a manifest that changes a name it binds. `DASHBOARD_VERSION` 2.11.2 → 2.11.3 (dotfile names in `CONFIG_EXTS` are categorized as config). `bin/tests.sh` 243 → 261 (new Tests 32 and 34); the declared gates stay at 12. **No phase, failure mode, quality gate, or workstream change.** **Adopters:** re-run `bin/sync`; an unreadable source manifest now stops with one line and a hint (`--source=local`) and writes nothing. Shipped as tag + GitHub Release `v4.2`, tagged at `f34769f`.
+- **v4.2:** **`--source=github` installs from the source's own manifest** — D8 of the parallel-sessions plan, the item v4.1 left out (PR #91; rmsharp's approval left three non-blocking points, all addressed before the merge on 2026-10-02). `bin/sync` and `bin/status` read the manifest of the repository they clone instead of this checkout's, so a source newer than the checkout installs its own file list. **The manifest is read as data, never run:** new `bin/_manifest_reader.py` parses the clone's `bin/_manifest.py` with `ast` and takes `DISTRIBUTION`, `SEED_FORMAT_MARKERS` and the two label strings as literals, which is why `_manifest.py` is documented as literal data, one plain assignment per name. **Unsafe rows are refused before anything is written:** a disposition other than this checkout's `tracked` or `seed` stops the run and names the rows (without it, a source labelling seeds differently would have its seeds written over an adopter's own copies; `bin/status` refuses the same way); a `src` or `dest` that is absolute, has a drive letter, climbs out with `..`, is or lies inside `.git`, names no file (`.`), or contains a NUL byte is refused, as is a manifest that changes a name it binds. `DASHBOARD_VERSION` 2.11.2 → 2.11.3 (dotfile names in `CONFIG_EXTS` are categorized as config). `bin/tests.sh` 243 → 261 (new Tests 32 and 34); the declared gates stay at 12. **No phase, failure mode, quality gate, or workstream change.** **Adopters:** update your methodology checkout, then re-run `bin/sync` (sync itself delivers only the 2.11.3 dashboard); with the updated checkout, an unreadable source manifest stops with one line and a hint (`--source=local`) and writes nothing. Shipped as tag + GitHub Release `v4.2`, tagged at `f34769f`.
